;; ADT-CYCLE-TLIST, and the cell that corrected its own first draft.
;;
;; Constructing the recursive arm with a real payload does NOT reach a
;; body-faithful VC. MEASURED, and the cause is not what a reader expects: it is
;; `constraint-symbols-unbound`, the `FQ-FREEVAR-GUARD-1` guard, and NOT the
;; §5.3.3 firewall. Emission produces a constraint naming a symbol its own
;; environment does not declare, and the guard withdraws the body VC whole.
;;
;; That distinction is the point of this cell. The construction path is closed by
;; a guard that catches a malformed constraint, not by a designed firewall. It is
;; the same accident that masked `carry-list.llmll` before v0.23.11, and
;; `PAIR-PROJ-LET-1` is the precedent for such an accident being removed. If a
;; later change repairs this free symbol, this path opens.
(export mk)
(type Tree (| Leaf) (| Node list[Tree]))
(def-shell mk [xs: list[Tree]] -> Tree
  (post (= result (Node xs)))
  (Node xs))
